-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I32 provider 1: the interface, the receiver type and its
-- impl.  The method carries a `Debug a =>` constraint; the standalone in `prov.mdk`
-- carries `Eq a =>` over a body of the same SHAPE, so the constraint set is the only
-- place the two schemes differ.
--
-- The impl body does NOT consume the method's own constraint dict, and that is a
-- requirement of this cell rather than a stylistic choice: an impl body that calls
-- `debug x` under this exact shadow makes `run` print the method's answer while the
-- BUILT BINARY dies `E-DISPATCH-NO-IMPL` at exit 1 -- a live engine split on a
-- separate axis (removing the collision, or the dict use, makes both agree).  A
-- fixture that carried both would be a row about two things and would grade RED for
-- the one it is not about.
public export data Box a = Box a

export interface Taggable t where
  tagOf : Debug a => t -> a -> String

export impl Taggable (Box b) where
  tagOf _ _ = "iface"
